
i.e.:

## These are the sourcefiles, being converted from html to adoc by 'pandoc'
curl https://logopraxis-institute.online/the-rolling-away-of-the-reproach-of-the-past-jos-chp-6/ |pandoc -f html -t asciidoc -o ch11.adoc

ln -sf ./ch11.adoc ./fromfile

cat ./fromfile |uconv --callback escape -f UTF-8 -t ASCII |grep -oP "%U[0-9A-F]{4}" |sort -u |cut -c '3-' |while read u; do printf "\\u$u :"; unicode $u |head -1; done
## reveals the following unicode characters in the file[s]:
– :U+2013 EN DASH
‘ :U+2018 LEFT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
’ :U+2019 RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK
“ :U+201C LEFT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK
” :U+201D RIGHT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK
… :U+2026 HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS
→ :U+2192 RIGHTWARDS ARROW

## which are replaced by/with: 
sed -Ei s/$'\u00A0'/' '/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u2013'/--/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u2014'/--/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u2018'/\'/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u2019'/\'/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u201C'/\"/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u201D'/\"/g fromfile && sed -Ei s/$'\u2026'/'...'/g fromfile


## the following file was already in the working directory
## from an earlier workflow which used 'lynx -dump' of the original sources, which stripped the italicization
ln -sf ../../Joshua-Millar/11-Rolling\ Away\ The\ Reproach\ Of\ The\ Past\ \(5\).adoc ./tofile

## What we're doing now is adding the _italicization_ to it
./add_italics  # 2>/dev/null to ignore the flood of error reports


The actual sequence has developed to:
-set the new files and links in place
-run the 'sed' chain on the ./fromfile
-then run the 'cat |uconv' on the .fromfile to confirm no lingering unicode there
-then run the 'cat |uconv' on the .tofile to discover any lingering unicode there; and then take steps to replace them

-THEN run the ./add_italics 
-then search the working file (./tofile link) for artifacts: i.e. '__' and '\w+_ _\w+' etc. (enclosed punctuation); newly displayed spelling errors caused by Canaanites being split by the italicization process
In fact, it would be helpful to check the fromfile for things like enclosed punctuation first == example: _Israel._ when reproduced within a sentance about some Israelites will make a bunch of '_Israel._tes'

Another good process revision would be to separate the creation of /tmp/italics from within the ./add_italics script in order to review it and locate short lines which end sentences with periods; and probably discard them with note-to-self to italicize them manually.




